// "Regenerate <permanent>" [CR#701.19a]: the next time it would be destroyed
// this turn, instead remove all damage marked on it and its controller taps
// it; if it's an attacking or blocking creature, remove it from combat. A
// resolving regeneration installs this single-use shield; only its eventual
// application carries the Regenerate label [CR#701.19c], so the declaration
// names no deed and the application (`regenerationApplication`) enacts it. The
// permanent is mentioned twice, so it is bound where the replacement's event
// first mentions it and read back by identity in the application.
KeywordAction(
    name: "regenerate",
    params: [Subject],
    spelling: "regenerate",
    grammar: Verb(
        bare: "regenerate",
        frame_set: Transitive,
    ),
    deed: None,
    body: replaceNextEvent(
        verbedEvent(Action("Destroy"), Param(0)),
        regenerationApplication(Param(0)),
        thisTurn,
    ),
)
